      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=3{x}^{4}+\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}+12.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we apply the addition, constant multiple, and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4}+\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}+12) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{-3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4})+4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 4{x}^{(4-1)}+4\\cdot (-3){x}^{(-3-1)}+0 \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}-12{x}^{-4} \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}-\\frac{12}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
